# services/ai-service/.dockerignore
#
# Everything not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon and lands in a layer that anyone who can
# pull the image can read — including every self-hoster. Deleting a file in a later RUN does not
# remove it from the earlier layer; `docker history` and `docker save` both still show it.

# ================================================================================================
# SECRETS AND ENVIRONMENT
# ================================================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ================================================================================================
# VIRTUALENVS — rebuilt by `uv sync --frozen` inside the image
# ================================================================================================
# Copying a host .venv in would shadow the frozen install with whatever the developer's machine
# resolved, and would do it silently — the image would then contain packages that appear in no
# SBOM and no lockfile. The compose dev overlay mounts an ANONYMOUS volume over /app/.venv for the
# same reason.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.python-version

# ================================================================================================
# MODEL WEIGHTS — never in a layer
# ================================================================================================
# BGE-M3, bge-reranker-v2-m3 and Docling's layout/table models are gigabytes each, appear in no
# SBOM, are invisible to pip-audit, and carry their own licences (Surya's weights are OpenRAIL-M
# while its code is Apache-2.0). They arrive on a mounted volume, pinned by COMMIT SHA in
# models.manifest.toml — never baked in from a developer's cache, where the revision is whatever
# `main` was that day.
models/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
.cache/
huggingface/

# ================================================================================================
# TESTS AND FIXTURES
# ================================================================================================
# Fixtures include the SSRF payload set, prompt-injection corpora and seeded credentials. None of
# that belongs in a shipped image.
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.coverage*

# ================================================================================================
# VCS, CI, EDITOR
# ================================================================================================
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# ================================================================================================
# DOCS AND LOCAL COMPOSE
# ================================================================================================
README.md
docs/
docker-compose*.yml
compose*.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   pyproject.toml, uv.lock   — the dependency graph; --frozen fails without both
#   models.manifest.toml      — the model licence + revision manifest the licence gate reads
